A||||4||Eric_PA||Help code 42 from ECM||||5||
Z||000000||Eric_PA||12-09-2001||11:27 AM||||Well just ran the codes in an 88 2.5 engine. I get the 42 error code which according to the book is an electronic advance timing error. What could cause this? Could it just be that we got a lot of rain and the car was ran through a puddle? The check engine light is no longer on, but was lit for about 5 minutes.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Eric||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||12-09-2001||12:09 PM||||Code 42 is set for several error conditions for the wires between the ECM and the ignition module mounted under the coils. Getting the engine wet could have caused it. I would check the 6 wire connector to the ignition module (under the coils) and look around for any exposed wires (usually from a wire rubbing against metal). If everything looks OK I wouldn't worry about it unless it does it again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-11-2001||08:44 AM||||Code 42 is most often caused by the ignition module or a bad ecm prom.  Could have been caused by getting wiring wet.  Clear codes by disconnecting battery for 10 sec. then don't worry about it unless it comes on again.<P>GTDude<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-11-2001||07:15 PM||||If it happened after going thru water, water got into something it probably should not have.<P>reset the ECM to erase the code.<P>pull the 2 plugs off the PIM and make sure thay are dry inside.<P>pull the plug wires off the coils and make sure there's no water in them. put some dielectric in the boots to keep out water.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eric_PA||12-11-2001||10:07 PM||||Thanks guys...<BR>The ECM was reset and still no error. It must have been the water, but if it happens again I will check all the connections.<P>Eric||||reg||10
